<!--
    "Call for help" (#144). A bell, and the one key on this keyboard that is
    allowed to be red.

    The premise everywhere else is that the only saturated colour on the surface
    is the category hue, because that hue carries meaning. This carries meaning
    too, and a different kind: it is the only control here that does something
    outside the text field, to somebody who is not in the room. It should not
    look like the keys around it, and it should be findable by a person who
    cannot read any of them.
-->
